##! # Effect Constants
##!
##! Single source of truth for effect type bitset values.
##! Effects are inferred bottom-up through the call graph via fixed-point
##! propagation. Multiple effects combine via bitwise OR.
##!
##! Used by: mir_lower_async_registry.qz, typecheck_walk.qz
##!
##! @see mir_lower_async_registry
##! @since 5.26.0

# === Effect Bitset ===

## No effects — function is pure (referentially transparent).
const EFFECT_NONE = 0

## I/O effect — reads/writes external state (puts, file_read, FFI calls).
const EFFECT_IO = 1

## Suspend effect — may yield execution (io_suspend, sched_yield, chan_recv).
const EFFECT_SUSPEND = 2

## Panic effect — may panic (panic(), bounds checks, unwrap on None).
const EFFECT_PANIC = 4

## Heap allocation effect — allocates heap memory (vec_new, hashmap_new, str_concat).
const EFFECT_ALLOC = 8

## All effects combined — used as conservative default for indirect calls and FFI.
const EFFECT_ALL = 15

## Sentinel: user explicitly annotated @pure. Distinct from EFFECT_NONE (which means
## "no annotation, infer effects"). When this bit is set, the compiler verifies that
## the inferred effects are EFFECT_NONE and emits QZ1410 if violated.
const EFFECT_ANNOTATED_PURE = 256
